  "unverified": [
    {
      "id": "B70",
      "reason": "No check available to this map can prove it. The {run} token is a property of a map a test-builder writes under the new runner, and this map must run under the current one, which does not expand {run}; the only artefact that could show it is a map produced by a test-builder dispatched inside a run, and no such artefact exists before the run. Provable once flight check expands {run} and a run has dispatched the test-builder against a sample launch."
    },
    {
      "id": "E18",
      "reason": "No deterministic check can produce it. The scribe returning assembled false requires dispatching the scribe against a launch with an input removed, which needs a model; the testbench has no probe harness and the conventions forbid a check that is not deterministic. Provable once a probe harness exists that can dispatch one subagent against a fixture, with a declared trials count and threshold."
    }
  ],
  "spec_findings": [
    {
      "node": "I8",
      "kind": "self-contradicting",
      "text": "I8 says explorer-return, worker-return, verifier-verdict and critic-findings are reused as they stand, and in the same breath that every return carries target: string and fix: int|null. All four schemas set additionalProperties false and carry neither field (worker-return carries unit, and no fix), so a return satisfying the universal sentence cannot validate against a schema reused as it stands. T27 holds the four to the fields they already carried and holds the seven new schemas to target and fix; it makes no claim either way about the four, and the fixtures for those four roles carry neither field."
    },
    {
      "node": "I13",
      "kind": "self-contradicting",
      "text": "I13 lists phase among the check-result fields kept 'as it stands', while D5 states a run has no phase field and I13 itself removes phase from the event line. No vocabulary of phase values survives anywhere in the spec, so a required field has no legal value. T49 asserts every other field of check-result and makes no claim about phase."
    },
    {
      "node": "I9",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "A fix dispatch is written to dispatches/<role>-<target>-fix-<k>.md, but the render signature in I5 is 'render <role> <target> [--fill <path>]' and fill.schema.json fixes six keys, none of which is the fix number. Nothing in the interfaces carries <k> to the renderer, so the filename cannot be produced by the interface as written. T9 asserts that a --fill previous_findings reaches the dispatch and makes no claim about the fix filename."
    },
    {
      "node": "C13",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "C13 requires a schema on every agent() call 'whose return it branches on'. Whether a return is branched on is not decidable from a script's text, and a scan that guessed would fail a compliant script. T42 scans the clauses that are decidable \u2014 the agentType on every call, an inline schema byte-equal to its file, no filesystem, shell, clock or chance, one level of nesting, a top-level return \u2014 and makes no claim about this one."
    },
    {
      "node": "I14",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "C13 forbids a workflow the filesystem and the shell, and I14 hands it only { launch, run, liftoff, entry } plus the steward. Yet fc-build must cut waves and units from plan.json (B31, B33) and fc-verify must find the sheet checks and rubrics of the pinned map (B51). No interface says how a workflow obtains the plan or the map. T37 and T38 read the dispatch pattern under a stub that answers a steward read with those documents, so an implementation that fetches them through the steward passes and one that finds another route passes too; the route itself stays unspecified."
    },
    {
      "node": "C2",
      "kind": "self-contradicting",
      "text": "C2 says flight install writes under .claude/ and CLAUDE.md only with --apply. I17 requires the same command to write the line 'flightdeck/.controlcenter' into .gitignore, which is neither. T44 allows .gitignore in the install boundary; on C2's wording alone that write is out of bounds."
    },
    {
      "node": "B4",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "B4 says flight run new creates runs/run-<n>/ 'with the I1 file set', and I1's set includes plan.json, plan.md, report.json and report.md, none of which can exist when a run opens. T4 asserts the containers I1 names \u2014 liftoff/, checks/, checks/rubrics/, evidence/, dispatches/, returns/ \u2014 and the two empty files B4 names, and makes no claim about the documents a later workflow writes."
    },
    {
      "node": "I1",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "fc lint spec reports 71 lint-artefacts errors, and the first group is this: I1, I4, I5, I13, I16 and VER name artefacts by bare file name or by a path relative to a launch folder \u2014 launch.json, plan.json, plan.md, report.json, report.md, specs/, runs/, liftoff/, checks/, rubrics/, evidence/, dispatches/, returns/, runs/run-1/checks/. A reader cannot resolve any of them from the text alone without first knowing which launch folder they hang from, and no rule can locate them in the repository. The checks read them against flightdeck/launch/<name>/, which is the reading I1's own tree implies, but the spec does not say it in the places that use the names."
    },
    {
      "node": "SC1",
      "kind": "imprecise",
      "text": "The second group of lint-artefacts errors is this: I2, I5, I8, I9, I11, I13, I14, I15, I16 and I17 name absolute paths that do not exist yet \u2014 flightdeck/flightcrew/bin/flight, the twelve schemas under flightdeck/flightcrew/schemas/run/, the nine workflow scripts, flightdeck/flightcrew/verify/, flightdeck/.controlcenter and the root CLAUDE.md. The scope domain names the folders these sit in but never the files, so nothing in the spec marks them as deliverables and the linter reads every one as a dangling reference. In a spec that builds its own tooling from nothing this is expected, but as written a reader cannot tell a path the run must create from a path it must already find."
    }
  ]
}
